# Layered Basic — slice 2 layeredEmit fixture
library "Layered Basic".

// A single multi-layer library: two `terminology` declarations (Concepts
// layer), two `coded from` concepts (Asserted layer), and one `defined as`
// concept (Inferred layer) composing over the asserted ones. Emitting this
// exercises the auto-split: the Inferred layer's bare refs to the asserted
// concepts MUST be re-qualified to "Layered Basic Asserted"."...", and the
// Asserted concepts' terminology refs MUST be re-qualified to
// "Layered Basic Concepts"."...".

// ============ Concepts (terminology) ============

terminology "Example Valueset A":
- valueset is `http://example.org/fhir/ValueSet/a`.

terminology "Example Valueset B":
- valueset is `http://example.org/fhir/ValueSet/b`.

// ============ Asserted (coded from) ============

concept "Asserted Concept A":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Example Valueset A".

concept "Asserted Concept B":
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- coded from "Example Valueset B".

// ============ Inferred (defined as) ============

concept "Inferred Concept":
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- defined as
(
   "Asserted Concept A"
   sem-or
   "Asserted Concept B"
).
